		{"id":"40dd703a89809baf","type":"text","text":"When the problem/opportunity remains vague, competing frames are unresolved, or new evidence contradicts the original framing","x":4815,"y":-2912,"width":420,"height":84,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"1c47676d8fe58e27","type":"file","file":"framework/Open Standards Main Map/Phase 1 Scope and Start/Decide On Aims and Objectives.md","x":5400,"y":-2739,"width":400,"height":73,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"47a855df1fdd0d30","type":"text","text":"When the causal pathway is weak, assumptions are doing too much work, or the standard’s expected mechanism of change is unclear","x":4815,"y":-2659,"width":420,"height":84,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"8f41eba134d6c866","type":"file","file":"framework/Open Standards Main Map/Phase 1 Scope and Start/1- Choose the Development Method.md","x":5400,"y":-2322,"width":400,"height":84,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"9187d7bf88bcab89","type":"text","text":"When the standard appears justified but phases, testing, infrastructure, roles, decision rights, or release logic are not ready","x":4815,"y":-2239,"width":420,"height":84,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"47c9737f054a3b79","type":"text","text":"When scope is too broad, too vague, or the essential feature set is not yet distinguishable from optional work","x":4815,"y":-2406,"width":420,"height":84,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"d49161f4bb78657d","type":"file","file":"framework/Open Standards Main Map/Phase 1 Scope and Start/Identify Core Features.md","x":5400,"y":-2389,"width":400,"height":50,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d0f61d311461a2d4","type":"text","text":"When the selected development approach does not match uncertainty, risk, participation needs, or legitimacy requirements","x":4815,"y":-2323,"width":420,"height":84,"color":"3"},
